_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.20577339880441312,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.04326127271964331,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.16755521706016754,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.07791,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":51.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.111,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":11.1,"pf":[],"description_full":"Arvinas, Inc., a clinical-stage biotechnology company, engages in the discovery, development, and commercialization of therapies to degrade disease-causing proteins. The company develops proteolysis targeting chimeras (PROTAC) targeted protein degraders that are designed to harness the body's own natural protein disposal system to degrade and remove disease-causing proteins. It is also developing clinical development programs, including ARV-102, a leucine-rich repeat kinase 2 (LRRK2) protein for the treatment of neurodegenerative diseases, such as Parkinson's disease and progressive supranuclear palsy; ARV-806, a Kirsten rat sarcoma G12D protein for the treatment of cancers with the G12D mutation comprising pancreatic, colorectal, and non-small cell lung cancer; ARV-393, a B-cell lymphoma 6 protein for the treatment of relapsed/refractory non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL); ARV-027, a polyglutamine-expanded androgen receptor in skeletal muscle; and vepdegestrant, an estrogen receptor for the treatment of locally advanced or metastatic ER+/HER2- breast cancer. In addition, the company develops Bavdegalutamide (ARV-110) and Luxdegalutamide (ARV-766), which are investigational orally bioavailable PROTAC protein degraders for the treatment of men with metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer. Arvinas, Inc. has collaborations with Pfizer Inc., Genentech, Inc., F. Hoffman-La Roche Ltd., Carrick Therapeutics Limited, and Bayer AG. The company was founded in 2013 and is based in New Haven, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Randy  Teel Ph.D. | CEO, President & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $711,098 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 246 people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 52%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $179K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Arvinas, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $447M market cap on $263M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +26% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","The company is burning through $276M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +26.9% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 20.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 17% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 7.8% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +26.9% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 45% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide"